I was very fortunate in the early game (somewhere in the 3000-4000
turns) range when I got a wand of wishing with 3 charges.  I used this
for the obligatory 2 blessed scrolls of charging, SDSM, gloves of
dexterity, and spellbook of identify.  It's incredible how much easier
the game is when you have a semi-reliable identification method.  I
later on used the wands to fill in some things I was missing but
didn't really need at that point (for instance, helm of brilliance).

Worst mistake I made was casting fireball and murdering a fellow gnome
when I had 9 points of protection and lost all of it. (later rebought)

I genocided krakens at the castle and Liches once I found the
vibrating square (I wanted a nice smooth ascension).

I had a really tight spot in Fire Plane... It seemed that a bunch of
the monsters had ways of summoning a ton of buddies.  At one point I
was 7 deep on all sides and that's when the amulet of life saving
saved me.  I used wands of teleportation and extrinsic speed to step
forward one space at a time and still almost got killed a second time.

I was also extraordinarily lucky that the first temple I picked was
the correct one.. I'm sure the riders would have been more challenging
if I had had to face them with no sps and no wand of death (for
pestilence/famine only, obviously).



